| 6 | Vetival | neat | 5 µL | 30 µL | B/C — vetiver-acetate function | Polishes the existing vetiver into a smoother, more tailored wood |
| 7 | Violet Leaf Absolute | 10% in DPG | 3 µL | 18 µL | C — iris-nitrile functional surrogate | Adds green-metallic rhizome realism and prevents flat lipstick powder |
| 8 | Alpha Ionone | neat | 3 µL | 18 µL | B — ionone-complex support | Adds a luminous woody-violet facet distinct from AIMI and beta-ionone |
| 9 | Allyl Ionone (Ketone V) | neat | 2 µL | 12 µL | C — ionone-complex expansion | Adds dry woody-violet movement and reduces one-note ionone compression |
| 10 | Dihydro Beta Ionone | neat | 1.5 µL | 9 µL | C — green woody ionone bridge | Connects pear, iris, cedar, and cocoa without adding more sweetness |
| 11 | Apritone | 10% stock | 3 µL | 18 µL | A/C — official pear effect | Soft apricot-pear skin nuance inside the ambrette accord |
| 12 | Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | 0.1% stock | 2 µL | 12 µL | A/C — official pear effect | High-impact juicy pear-liqueur sparkle at trace active dose |
| 13 | Cocoa CO2 Extract | 7.7% stock | 3 µL | 18 µL | D — interpretive cacao micro-accent | Adds cocoa-butter realism without creating a chocolate perfume |
| 14 | Farnesol | as supplied | 2 µL | 12 µL | A — official INCI supported | Soft floral-fatty continuity and naturalistic blending |
| 15 | Geraniol | 10% in DPG | 2 µL | 12 µL | A — official INCI supported | Trace rosy floral lift present in the label evidence |
| 16 | Citronellol | 10% working dilution | 5 µL | 30 µL | A — official INCI supported | Trace rosy-citrus softness without making a rose note |
| 17 | Lilyreal ND | as supplied; verify bottle strength | 4 µL | 24 µL | A/C — historical muguet-label substitute | Restores a small classic muguet bridge without using the restricted Lilial stock |
|  | **Expansion total** |  | **90 µL** | **540 µL** |  |  |

The 40-row source plus these 17 genuinely new rows yields a 57-row expanded formula. That happens to match the ingredient count advertised by the secondary GC-MS archive, but the matching count does **not** prove that the identities or doses are the same.

## Stock preparation

Prepare Citronellol at 10% before dosing:

```text
100 µL neat Citronellol
+ 900 µL DPG
= 1,000 µL Citronellol 10%
```

Use 5 µL of this working dilution per 1,000 µL existing concentrate, or 30 µL for 6,000 µL existing concentrate.

Orris Liquid and Lilyreal ND are dosed as supplied. Their internal strength is not fully specified in the inventory, so verify their labels before scaling.

## What each block corrects

### 1. Natural iris and iris-nitrile gap

Orris Liquid, Violet Leaf Absolute 10%, Alpha Ionone, Allyl Ionone, and Dihydro Beta Ionone add rhizome, green-metallic, woody, and diffusive facets around the existing large ionone block. They do not reproduce Iris Nitrile chemically; they are a functional reconstruction from available stock.

### 2. Ambrette and pear gap

Ambrettolide 10%, Apritone 10%, and Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate 0.1% create the musky, slightly fruity 'pear liqueur and silk talc' character that Dior publicly associates with ambrette seed.

### 3. Citrus-aromatic detail

Cedrat FCF, Lemon FCF, and trace Ginger create the more detailed top architecture reported by the secondary GC-MS source without overpowering the existing lavender and bergamot.

### 4. Polished wood and musk

Vetival adds the vetiver-acetate-style polish missing from the existing natural vetiver line. Ambrettolide adds a distinct macrocyclic musk texture rather than merely increasing Galaxolide.

### 5. Label-supported floral traces

Farnesol, Geraniol 10%, and Citronellol 10% are added at trace levels because they appear in Dior's public ingredient label and soften the iris-lavender transition.

### 6. Historical muguet bridge

Lilyreal ND is a small practical replacement for the older Lilial-type muguet effect. Do not use the inventory's Lilial in a skin perfume merely for historical fidelity.

### 7. Cocoa micro-accent

Cocoa CO2 7.7% is deliberately microscopic. Cocoa is not part of Dior's current official 2011 note description; it is an interpretive nod to the older Dior Homme Intense/cacao discourse and to the cocoa-butter illusion many people perceive from iris, ambrette, cedar, and vanillic materials. The dose is designed to add texture, not a chocolate note.

## Addition order

Add to the already-mixed concentrate in this order:

1. Ambrettolide 10%, Vetival, Cocoa CO2 7.7%, Farnesol, and Orris Liquid.
2. Alpha Ionone, Allyl Ionone, Dihydro Beta Ionone, Violet Leaf Absolute 10%, and Lilyreal ND.
3. Apritone 10%, Citronellol 10%, Geraniol 10%, Ginger EO, Cedrat FCF, Lemon FCF, and Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate 0.1%.
4. Mix thoroughly and rest the concentrate at least 72 hours before dilution or further correction.

